## 📱 Responsive Design

The website uses a media query for screens with a maximum width of `768px`.

On smaller screens:

* Cards are displayed in a single column
* Images and videos adapt to the available width
* Text and navigation elements become smaller
* The main sections adjust their spacing
* The YouTube video keeps its 16:9 aspect ratio

## 🎨 Colour Palette

| Colour     | Hex code  | Purpose                         |
| ---------- | --------- | ------------------------------- |
| Dark black | `#0D0B08` | Main background                 |
| Soft black | `#141210` | Footer and secondary background |
| Gold       | `#D4AF37` | Titles, icons, and highlights   |
| Light gold | `#F0CC5C` | Hover effects                   |
| Dark red   | `#8B1E1E` | Buttons                         |
| Light red  | `#A82A2A` | Button hover effects            |
| Off-white  | `#E8E4DA` | Main text                       |
| Cream      | `#F5F1E8` | Card background                 |

## 🚀 Running the Project

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/v1ctorx/Fake-Web-site-practicing-.git
```

Enter the project directory:

```bash
cd Fake-Web-site-practicing-
```

Open `index.html` in your browser.

You can also run the project with the **Live Server** extension in Visual Studio Code.

